1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:05,220
从浩瀚太空俯瞰东亚大陆，北纬31°，
From deep space, we look down on East Asia at 31° north.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:09,340
正是万里长江奔流入海的终点。
Here the mighty Yangtze reaches the sea.

3
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:13,980
六千三百公里江水裹挟着上游带来的泥沙，
The Yangtze carries silt from upstream along its 6,300-kilometer course,

4
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:18,260
在东海之滨与潮汐昼夜激荡。
churning day and night with the tides of the East China Sea.

5
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:24,780
六千年前，今日繁华的上海大半还沉睡在波涛之下；
Six thousand years ago, most of modern Shanghai slumbered beneath the waves;

6
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:32,780
岁月的冲积，让三条古海岸线步步向东延伸，沧海终成桑田。
Sedimentation pushed three ancient coastlines eastward, turning sea into land.

7
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:39,260
战国春申君黄歇疏治水脉，“黄浦”与“申”自此结缘；
Lord Chunshen dredged the waterways, birthing the names 'Huangpu' and 'Shen';

8
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:46,280
先民在吴淞江下游列竹捕鱼，更赋予了这片水乡“沪”的古称。
bamboo fishing traps along Wusong River gave rise to 'Hu'.

9
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:51,500
及至宋元明初，水系历经“黄浦夺淞”的历史巨变，
From the Song era to the early Ming, the river system underwent the Huangpu’s capture of the Wusong.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:59,600
浩荡黄浦江跃升为主干大江，奠定了上海“一江一河”的千年骨架。
The Huangpu became the main river, shaping Shanghai?s enduring river-and-creek framework.

11
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:06,020
公元一二九二年，元朝在黄浦江西岸正式设立上海县，
In 1292, the Yuan court established Shanghai County on the west bank of the Huangpu,

12
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:12,400
这座枕江濒海的江南聚落，自此登上了中华城市文明的历史舞台。
bringing this riverside Jiangnan settlement onto the historical stage.

13
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,260
凭借舟楫之便与闻名天下的松江棉布，
River transport and renowned Songjiang cotton textiles helped trade flourish;

14
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:22,360
这片江海沙嘴迅速崛起了生气勃勃的江南水畔市镇。
a vibrant Jiangnan port town rapidly rose along the estuary.

15
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:27,200
第一章：九里环城与江南名邑。明清两代，
Chapter 1: The Walled City and Jiangnan Gem. In the Ming and Qing eras,

16
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:34,960
上海在黄浦江西岸筑起坚城，成长为繁盛一时的“江海之通津”。
Shanghai raised a circular fortress on the west bank of the Huangpu.

17
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:43,000
明嘉靖三十二年，为抵御倭患，上海仅用两个月便筑起周长九里的环形城墙；
In the 32nd year of Jiajing (1553), a nine-li wall was built in just two months to resist coastal raiders.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,440
护城河碧波环抱，六座城楼巍然耸立，城内粉墙黛瓦鳞次栉比。
A moat encircled six gate towers, with white walls and dark-tiled homes packed within.

19
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:55,660
在这座环形城池的东北隅，明代潘允端为奉养双亲，
In the city’s northeast, Ming official Pan Yunduan built a garden to honor his parents.

20
00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:00,780
历时十八载营建了名震江南的私家园林——豫园。
Eighteen years of work created the renowned private garden, Yu Garden.

21
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:09,520
步入园中，九曲朱栏桥蜿蜒卧波，八角重檐的湖心亭飞檐翘角倒映碧水，
The zigzag vermilion bridge and the double-eaved Huxinting Pavilion are reflected in the pond.

22
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:14,680
四周白墙黛瓦游廊与奇峰假山交相辉映。
White-walled galleries, dark tiles and dramatic rockeries complete the scene.

23
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:20,360
从豫园飞檐抬升东望，越过城内连绵的黛瓦屋脊，
Rising east from Yu Garden, we pass above the city’s continuous dark-tiled rooftops.

24
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:26,020
穿出大东门城楼，迎面便是紧邻黄浦江岸的十六铺古码头。
Beyond the Great East Gate lies Shiliupu Wharf, beside the Huangpu River.

25
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:31,440
清代康熙开海设关后，十六铺木栈码头绵延里许，
After maritime trade reopened under Kangxi, Shiliupu’s timber wharves stretched along the shore.

26
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:39,860
三千余艘平底沙船与远洋商船在此昼夜停泊，帆樯如林，万商云集。
More than 3,000 sand junks and ocean-going ships gathered here, their masts forming a forest.

27
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:45,700
一座内有粉墙园林、外通四海舟楫的“东南都会”，
A southeastern metropolis, with gardens within and maritime trade beyond,

28
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,880
已然在黄浦江西岸蔚然成形。
had taken shape on the western bank of the Huangpu.

29
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:55,980
第二章：十里洋场与海派风华。一八四三年上海开埠，
Chapter 2: The Bund and Haipai Elegance. After opening in 1843,

30
00:02:55,980 --> 00:03:06,940
城市重心自老城厢顺黄浦江西岸一路向北延伸，直抵吴淞江汇入黄浦江的河口。
the urban center expanded north from the Old City along the Huangpu to Suzhou Creek.

31
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:16,340
在吴淞江与黄浦江交汇的河口，一九〇七年落成的外白渡桥以双跨全钢桁架横跨碧波，
At the mouth of Suzhou Creek, the 1907 Waibaidu Bridge spanned the waters with twin steel trusses,

32
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:20,280
拉开了近代市政与工业文明的序幕。
heralding modern municipal engineering.

33
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:26,080
顺着外白渡桥向南延展的一点五公里弧形江岸上，
Stretching 1.5 kilometers south from Waibaidu Bridge,

34
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:34,860
数十座古典花岗岩大厦临江而立，筑起了举世闻名的“外滩万国建筑博览群”。
dozens of granite edifices rose along the river bend to form the legendary Bund.

35
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:41,320
南京东路口的和平饭店以八角绿铜金字塔顶傲立江岸，
At Nanjing Road stands the Peace Hotel's emerald copper pyramid,

36
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:49,400
紧邻其南的江海关大楼则以希腊多立克柱廊托起高耸的四面发光大钟楼。
To its south, the Customs House pairs a Doric colonnade with a glowing four-faced clock tower.

37
00:03:49,400 --> 00:04:00,200
再往南移，原汇丰银行大楼以严谨的三段式对称花岗岩立面、六根科林斯巨柱与威严的古罗马大穹顶，
The former HSBC Building has a symmetrical granite facade, six Corinthian columns and a grand Roman-style dome.

38
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:04,120
尽显远东金融街的恢弘气象。
Together they project the grandeur of the Far East’s financial quarter.

39
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:09,920
从外滩金融长廊顺着南京路向西步入浦西腹地，
Gliding west from the Bund along Nanjing Road into inland Puxi,

40
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:20,860
成片红青砖相间、灰瓦双坡顶的石库门里弄星罗棋布，巴洛克雕花门楣下围合着江南天井。
rows of red-and-grey brick Shikumen lanes unfold with pitched roofs and carved stone gates.

41
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:27,820
十里南京路霓虹闪耀，万国建筑与石库门街巷交相辉映，
Nanjing Road’s neon, international-style buildings and Shikumen lanes illuminate one another.

42
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:33,860
共同孕育出开放包容、中西交融的海派都市文化。
Together they nurtured an open Haipai culture, blending Chinese and Western influences.

43
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:41,720
第三章：星火觉醒与工业脊梁。当镜头深入浦西中南部的石库门街网，
Chapter 3: Awakening Spark and Industrial Backbone. Deep within the Shikumen grid of central Puxi,

44
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:48,500
救亡图存的时代火种正在静谧的里弄间悄然汇聚。
the spark of national awakening quietly gathered.

45
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:57,200
一九二一年夏，在兴业路七十六号这座青红砖相间、雕花石框门头的石库门小楼里，
In the summer of 1921, inside the red-and-grey brick Shikumen house at 76 Xingye Road,

46
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:04,640
中国共产党的诞生如东方破晓，点燃了改写民族命运的燎原星火。
the birth of the CPC ignited a spark that changed China's destiny.

47
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:11,500
一九四九年五月，红旗漫卷黄浦江两岸，上海迎来历史新生，
In May 1949, Shanghai greeted a new dawn along both banks of the Huangpu,

48
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:18,580
昔日的十里洋场自此转型为撑起共和国脊梁的现代工业基地。
transforming into the industrial powerhouse of the young Republic.

49
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:25,620
顺着黄浦江向南岸工业带望去，江南造船厂的巨型龙门吊巍然耸立，
Along the southern Huangpu industrial belt, giant gantry cranes towered over Jiangnan Shipyard,

50
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:33,220
中国第一台万吨水压机与第一艘国产万吨远洋巨轮先后在此诞生。
birthing China's first 10,000-ton hydraulic press and ocean freighter.

51
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:39,900
国产万吨巨轮在黄浦江主航道上劈波斩浪、鸣笛远航，
Locally built 10,000-ton ocean vessels cleaved the waves of the Huangpu,

52
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:45,640
“上海制造”更化作自力更生与精益求精的时代丰碑。
making 'Made in Shanghai' a monument of self-reliance and excellence.

53
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:52,780
至八十年代末，黄浦江西岸的浦西已是广厦千间、百业兴旺；
By the late 1980s, Puxi on the west bank was densely built and thriving,

54
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:59,020
而一江之隔的浦东陆家嘴，仍是一片静候春风的江东沙嘴。
while across the river, Pudong's Lujiazui peninsula awaited the spring wind.

55
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:07,840
第四章：跨江东进与浦东奇迹。一九九〇年春，开发开放浦东的号角吹响，
Chapter 4: Crossing the River. In spring 1990, the call to develop and open Pudong sounded.

56
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:15,400
上海终于迈出了从浦西跨越黄浦江、向东拥抱太平洋的历史性一步。
Shanghai took a historic step east across the Huangpu, toward the Pacific.

57
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:20,520
雄伟的斜拉索跨江大桥与越江隧道飞架东西，
Cable-stayed bridges and tunnels linked both banks,

58
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:29,020
宽阔的世纪大道在陆家嘴半岛铺展延伸，拉开了现代摩天都会的宏伟蓝图。
while Century Avenue unfurled across the Lujiazui peninsula to launch a modern metropolis.

59
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:35,040
一九九四年，在陆家嘴半岛最前端与外滩隔江相望处，
In 1994, at the tip of Lujiazui, across the river from the Bund,

60
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:43,920
高四百六十八米的东方明珠塔率先拔地而起，十一颗璀璨球体如“大珠小珠落玉盘”。
the 468-meter Oriental Pearl Tower rose, its eleven spheres evoking pearls on a jade plate.

61
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:53,300
一九九九年，顺着陆家嘴核心区向东推进，高四百二十点五米的金茂大厦拔地而起，
In 1999, farther east in central Lujiazui, the 420.5-meter Jin Mao Tower rose.

62
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:58,740
十六节退台式塔身将中华古塔神韵融入现代钢骨玻璃。
Its sixteen tiered setbacks blend the spirit of ancient pagodas with modern steel and glass.

63
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:07,340
二〇〇八年，紧邻金茂大厦东南侧，高四百九十二米的上海环球金融中心凌空矗立，
In 2008, southeast of Jin Mao, the 492-meter Shanghai World Financial Center rose.

64
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:11,840
顶部梯形风洞天桥如利剑划破云端。
Its trapezoidal opening and skybridge cut a distinctive profile against the clouds.

65
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:21,160
二〇一五年，高六百三十二米的上海中心大厦以一百二十度柔和螺旋扶摇直上，
In 2015, the 632-meter Shanghai Tower rose in a gentle 120-degree spiral,

66
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:25,060
与金茂、环球鼎足而立，问鼎中国第一高楼。
joining Jin Mao and the World Financial Center as China’s tallest building.

67
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:32,020
短短三十余年间，数百座现代摩天大楼在浦东聚木成林，
Within just three decades, hundreds of modern skyscrapers formed a vertical forest in Pudong,

68
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:39,880
与西岸百年外滩隔江辉映，共同谱写出世界城市史上的东方奇迹。
shining across the river from the historic Bund.

69
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:46,180
终章：古今交响与星辰大海。当金色暮霭轻拂浦江两岸，
Epilogue: Symphony of Millennia. As golden dusk caresses both banks of the Huangpu,

70
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:52,960
上海六千年的地理成陆与建筑文明在这一刻璀璨同辉。
six thousand years of geography and architecture shine in unison.

71
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:57,480
站在四百多年的豫园湖心亭飞檐下极目东望，
Looking east from beneath the historic upturned eaves of Huxinting,

72
00:07:57,480 --> 00:08:06,140
古典江南的黛瓦九曲桥与陆家嘴直插云霄的摩天巨塔跨越时空深情对话。
Jiangnan’s tiled pavilions and zigzag bridge converse across time with Lujiazui’s soaring towers.

73
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:11,900
黄浦江与苏州河世界级滨水岸线全线贯通，
Continuous waterfront promenades now connect the urban banks of the Huangpu and Suzhou Creek.

74
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:18,000
左岸是百年峥嵘的近代记忆，右岸是拔地而起的时代华章。
the left bank preserves a century of memory while the right bank writes a new era.

75
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:22,980
海纳百川，追求卓越；开明睿智，大气谦和。
Inclusive, excellent, open-minded and wise; magnanimous and modest.

76
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:29,320
这十六字城市精神，早已镌刻进上海的每一寸街巷与天际。
this city spirit is etched into every lane and skyline of Shanghai.

77
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:34,740
从六千年前的江海沙嘴，到今日傲立东方的全球大都市，
From an ancient coastal sandbar six millennia ago to a global metropolis of the East,

78
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:42,200
上海正迎着太平洋的浩荡长风，驶向更加壮阔的星辰大海。
Shanghai sails on the Pacific winds toward a boundless future.
